Body:
OpenCode Go serves DeepSeek and Kimi only via /v1/chat/completions. Both providers also have Anthropic-compatible endpoints, which would fix the Claude Code tool-calling issues by eliminating the protocol translation layer entirely (see #24722, #26331)

- **DeepSeek**: `https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic` [Official DeepSeek Documentation](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/anthropic_api)
- **Kimi**: `https://api.moonshot.ai/anthropic` Moonshot [officially instructs](https://platform.kimi.ai/docs/guide/agent-support#using-kimi-k2-5-model-in-claude-code) Claude Code users to use this. Formal API reference is pending (MoonshotAI/Kimi-K2#129), but the endpoint is functional and officially supported.

This is a zero-code config change. The schema at `packages/console/core/src/model.ts:33` already supports `formatFilter` for dual-format models. Qwen 3.6 Plus already works this way (both `/v1/messages` and `/v1/chat/completions`). The `anthropicHelper` and body converter (`provider.ts:182-185`) are transparent proxies when formats match.

What's needed is to add two provider entries and formatFilter additions in the Go model data (`ZEN_MODELS*` secrets):

```diff
+ "deepseek-anthropic": {api: "https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic", format: "anthropic", ...}
+ "moonshot-anthropic": {api: "https://api.moonshot.ai/anthropic", format: "anthropic", ...}

  "deepseek-v4-pro": [
    {formatFilter: "oa-compat", providers: [{id: "deepseek", ...}]},
+   {formatFilter: "anthropic", providers: [{id: "deepseek-anthropic", model: "deepseek-v4-pro"}]}
  ]
  // same pattern for deepseek-v4-flash, kimi-k2.5, kimi-k2.6, etc.
```
